{
  "rationale": "The authorised evidence (entityR2A, the race of iteration 1, score 525.5) shows a clear split. The oval is solved: 20 of 20 finished, with rms_error 0.012 m and 0.1 line-loss events per run. The s-bend finishes only 8 of 20 (12 off track), and the slalom never finishes (all 20 off track at progress 0.18, max_error 0.064 m, 2 line-loss events). The failures are off-track exits on the tight, sharp sections, not stalls or oscillation: steering_oscillation (0.23 to 0.31) and rms_error (0.018 to 0.033 m) are moderate. Body width cannot widen the off-track limit: max(0.06, 0.0125 + body_width/4) stays at the 0.06 m floor across the whole allowed range, so I am not changing it. The levers left are sensor geometry and drive agility. Wheel track sets yaw rate for a given wheel-speed difference (turn rate = wheel speed difference / wheel_track), so a narrower track gives more turn per unit of controller command on the sharp slalom bends. I therefore change one drive parameter: wheel_track 0.12 m to 0.10 m. I keep the iteration-1 sensor array (16 mm footprints, 12 mm spacing, y 0.05 m), mass 0.5 kg and wheel radius 0.03 m, so any change in results can be attributed to the track width. Expected result: the slalom progress rises above the 0.18 mark and the s-bend finish rate improves, with line_loss_events staying near the current level. The main risk is wheel slip or saturation at higher turn rates, which the Integrator should check through control_effort and steering_oscillation.",
  "geometry": {
    "body_length": 0.18,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "mass": 0.5,
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": 0.024, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.012, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.012, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.024, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.016,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "wheel_track": 0.10
  },
  "intent": "Keep the iteration-1 sensing array and mass, which already complete the oval reliably, and narrow the wheel track from 0.12 m to 0.10 m to increase yaw authority on the sharp s-bend and slalom sections where the robot currently leaves the tape. Expected result: slalom progress above 0.18 and a higher s-bend finish rate, with the oval still completing. This is a single-parameter change on the drive geometry so its effect can be read cleanly.",
  "feedback_request": {
    "questions": [
      "Does the narrower 0.10 m track give the controller enough turn rate on the slalom without saturating the wheel commands (check control_effort and whether the wheels hit the +/-4095 limit)?",
      "On which track and at what progress does the robot now leave the line: is the slalom failure point moved further along the course than 0.18?",
      "Does the narrower track cause steering_oscillation to rise on the oval, which currently completes cleanly?",
      "Are line_loss_events still 2 or more on the slalom, and do they occur at the same bend each time?",
      "If the slalom still fails, would you prefer a forward sensor offset (y toward 0.06 to 0.07 m) or a wider 7-sensor array as the next change?"
    ]
  },
  "learning": "Iteration 1 (score 525.5) moved the robot from off-track failures at progress 0.1 to 0.15 to a finishing oval and a partly finishing s-bend. The slalom remains the limit. Next, if the narrower track helps, test a forward sensor offset to add lookahead; if it hurts oscillation, return to 0.12 m and test sensor offset instead."
}
